    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46074" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζά̆κορ-ος</span></b> , ὁ and ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>attendant in a temple</i> (more honourable than <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νεωκόρος</span> acc. to Philem.Lex. (cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Philol.</u>
				57.353
			</span></i> sqq.) in Reitzenstein <i>Gesch.d.Gr.Etym.</i><i><span class="en">
				p.394
			</span></i>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζ. Ἀφροδίτης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hyp.
					<u>Fr.</u>
					178
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Cam.</u>
					30
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δηοῦς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					3.713.1
				</span></i>
			: abs., <i><span class="en">
				Anon.
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				218ii14
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰς ἱερείας καὶ τὰς ζ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					12.4.14
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(v B.C.)</span>, cf. ib.<i><span class="en">
				7.1883
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Thespiae</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				126
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				311
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(2).484.21
			</span></i> (Mytil., late), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Sull.</u>
				7
			</span></i>, etc.</div>
